{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#123","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#123","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#123\",\"parent_revision\":\"d623681a055efc272b03201e5983352b223064ee30ecbd4d7073fe0ce0ff15ca\",\"root_revision\":\"d623681a055efc272b03201e5983352b223064ee30ecbd4d7073fe0ce0ff15ca\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEvery `packages/skilllint/rules/*_series.py` defines a private `_docs_url(code)` that now just wraps `rule_reference(code)` and has **zero call sites**. PR #108 replaced the call sites but left the wrappers in place.\\n\\nRuff does not flag them \u2014 module-level functions are not unused-variable candidates \u2014 so they are invisible to the existing gates.\\n\\nTwelve identical dead functions: a DRY violation that outlived the duplication it was extracted from.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nOne-line-per-file deletion.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Overlap To Check First\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPR #103 is titled \\\"deduplicate `_docs_url`\\\". Whoever picks this up should read #103 before starting \u2014 it may already do this work, in which case this issue closes with that PR rather than a new one.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #108 \u2014 introduced `rule_reference`, left the wrappers\\n- #103 \u2014 possibly-overlapping open PR\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5cf578911369ca222cf6ec1638e1d94356bbd6ad002999aa9b70f79c3edff9bd\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-8vA\"}"}